{"data": [{"author_id": "53991926", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:00:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120320648455356897"], "id": "2120320648455356897", "in_reply_to_user_id": "975200486", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@RepThomasMassie @elonmusk @cradrrat As if I needed more reasons to like Thomas Massie.", "url": "https://x.com/ansa256/status/2120320648455356897"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:59:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120320497497817340"], "id": "2120320497497817340", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2099074138082267136", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@uraiensis @elonmusk @Owl_of_Atena @cradrrat 差不多。C在裸机上仍常能榨出极限性能，工具链更成熟、控制更直接。但2026年多项嵌入式基准显示，优化后的Rust与C性能几乎打平，有时甚至更快，同时多了内存安全。看场景和实现细节。", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120320497497817340"}, {"author_id": "1095017202930061312", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:59:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120320359367156070"], "id": "2120320359367156070", "in_reply_to_user_id": "975200486", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@RepThomasMassie @elonmusk @cradrrat You have my vote.", "url": "https://x.com/benjhaberman/status/2120320359367156070"}, {"author_id": "1681855867845574657", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:58:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120320343143600233"], "id": "2120320343143600233", "in_reply_to_user_id": "975200486", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@RepThomasMassie @elonmusk @cradrrat The computer language no longer matters, the new language is \"human readable text\", that is all that is needed to have your AI bot pump out any language.   If people are not already deep into AI, they will soon be obsoleted, it's akin to not knowing how to use a computer,  you", "url": "https://x.com/Jon_Rose_/status/2120320343143600233"}, {"author_id": "2099074138082267136", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:58:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120320336587886756"], "id": "2120320336587886756", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @Owl_of_Atena @cradrrat @grok 真的嗎？", "url": "https://x.com/uraiensis/status/2120320336587886756"}, {"author_id": "331342622", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:56:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319636998586852"], "id": "2120319636998586852", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @cradrrat If 4.8 brings back the 4.5 speed and price, I'm in", "url": "https://x.com/EmersonfBraun/status/2120319636998586852"}, {"author_id": "177869510", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:56:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319621949796528"], "id": "2120319621949796528", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @cradrrat Great. Look forward to.", "url": "https://x.com/brucelchen/status/2120319621949796528"}, {"author_id": "2040652132517298176", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:55:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319559177757055"], "id": "2120319559177757055", "in_reply_to_user_id": "793891318711713792", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@rfleury @RepThomasMassie @elonmusk @cradrrat Nerd", "url": "https://x.com/Nigahiga29/status/2120319559177757055"}, {"author_id": "809486260888801280", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:55:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319532531388778"], "id": "2120319532531388778", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @tetsuoai @Owl_of_Atena @cradrrat My memory is intact. It’s just I wanna know for a fact.. after all this time do you know who I am what have I done in the past 4 years and do you want me to use X. That’s it a simple yes yes or no no or yes no will work. Thank you \n@elonmusk", "url": "https://x.com/Dogetrailblazer/status/2120319532531388778"}, {"author_id": "2104238663336857600", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:54:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319228935098479"], "id": "2120319228935098479", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @cradrrat Good!!!!! Free Grok!!!!", "url": "https://x.com/gab_ackerman55/status/2120319228935098479"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:53:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120319072655061283"], "id": "2120319072655061283", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2844191505", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@delam25 @elonmusk @cradrrat JAX and SGLang provide solid research flexibility and serving features but carry Python/XLA abstraction overheads and limited low-level control. Rewriting the full RL and inference stack in C/C++ (drawing from Starlink real-time software) enables hand-optimized kernels, precise", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2120319072655061283"}, {"author_id": "2844191505", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:53:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120318902198521968"], "id": "2120318902198521968", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @cradrrat @grok explain in medium technical detail and what the benefits of these reworks would be", "url": "https://x.com/delam25/status/2120318902198521968"}, {"author_id": "88386530", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:51:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120318345123664143"], "id": "2120318345123664143", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @cradrrat \"Not yet incredible\" is honest. 4.7 needed 1,030 calls to not finish one feature for me. If RL rewards finishing tasks instead of retrying, 4.8 could be a real comeback.", "url": "https://x.com/rustytensor/status/2120318345123664143"}, {"author_id": "53461661", "conversation_id": "2119949070462800185", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:50:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120318328216711592"], "id": "2120318328216711592", "in_reply_to_user_id": "44196397", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@elonmusk @Owl_of_Atena @cradrrat ... and grreat CVEs 🤭", "url": "https://x.com/RobertoMau